      "defers the manaSource phase past targeting when the cost scales with targets",
      "keeps costPayment before targeting when the threshold is printed, not derived",
      "keeps manaSource before targeting for an ordinary spell",
      "offers the tap step but leaves auto-tap alone",
      "opens a hand selection phase and exposes the eligible green card",
      "opens manual payment even when auto-tap is enabled so life is selectable",
      "opens manual payment for a Phyrexian-only cost with no mana sources",
      "picks the sacrifice BEFORE manual mana-source selection, since it changes the cost owed",
      "plain choose-N modal (Spree) runs only the modalModes phase",
      "prices the picker on the targets the caster chose",
      "runs no manaSource phase at all under auto-tap — the server prices the targets",
      "runs the evidence picker after targeting, never before",
      "runs the sacrifice step exactly once when auto-tap handles the mana",
      "still runs manual mana selection after the taps when auto-tap is off",
      "submits the chosen card through additionalCostPayment.exiledCards",
      "waterbend gets the same treatment — the taps do not force a mana-source confirm"
    ],
    "web-client/src/store/slices/ui/publicTargetGroups.test.ts": [
      "keeps mode and splice choices unchanged",
      "later cost merge preserves captured public groups",
      "legacy flat phase does not invent a group boundary",
      "retains an omitted original group before a later choice",
      "retains separate occurrences of the same recipient",
      "revising an earlier requirement preserves only the revised groups",
      "saves the omitted group before calling the legacy phase entrypoint"
    ],
    "web-client/src/store/slices/ui/targetingSlice.test.ts": [
      "confirming a requirement snapshots it for goBackTargeting",
      "confirming the last requirement submits all picks in requirement order",
      "goBackTargeting is a no-op on the first requirement",
      "goBackTargeting restores the previous requirement with its picks selected",
      "re-confirming after a revised pick re-filters the next requirement"
